 "comment": "Western sources -> cards. Spec 2026-10-27-melody-trained-design. PDMX: a row goes to every card whose rule matches its genres (PDMX genre field split on '-'), tags (split on '-'), words (a regex prefix on the ASCII-folded title, song name and tags) or composers (a whole-word regex on composer and artist). tier 0 = a specific match (a composer, a dance name, a national tag), tier 1 = a broad genre fallback; up to 600 pieces per card, tier 0 first. Cards without a rule (or without matches) get no PDMX material and fall back to the grammar. Hand-set judgements; tune by ear.",
